WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.940
It’s been a while since I’ve ridden a horse, but Andrea has lent me the lovely Annie today.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.000
We're going to ride one of
our beautiful Beach trails.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.880
The Northern Pegasus Bay Bylaw has a few rules you need to be aware of

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.040
when riding horses along the coastal strip.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.800
Firstly, we need to stay on the designated horse trails

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.680
and give way to people on foot at all
times.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.320
When we’re on the beach itself, we need to stay in the designated areas.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:37.840
For horse riders most of the coastal strip is fine, but the Ashley-Rakahuri Estuary is off-limits.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.520
We also need to stay below the last high tide mark

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.000
unless we’re using an access trail or avoiding a potentially unsafe situation.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.160
And finally, don’t ride through any surf life-saving areas.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.120
So it’s not too hard, it all comes down to basic commonsense and courtesy for others.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.840
We’ve all got a part to play in preserving our beaches &amp; estuary.

